#DESCRIPTION
Dissociative recombination O2+ + e -> O + O in a full (semi-implicit) PIC plasma
with kinetic electrons, n_e = n_i = 5 /cc. k(Te) = 0.4*(2500/Te)^0.5 = 0.2 cm^3/s
at Te = 1e4 K, k*n0*T = 2. Analytic: n(t) = n0/(1 + k*n0*t) for both the ions and
the electrons. n_e and Te must be taken from the particles, not UNIFORMSTATE.

